Code statements information:
The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
update_rw_regs(host, 1, true, cw);
config_nand_cw_read(chip, false, cw);
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because when the number of code words is set to 1, the QPIC controller misinterprets this as a request to read the last code word. The original code does not account for the separate register introduced in QPIC V2 for reading the last code word, leading to incorrect data being read.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
update_rw_regs(host, 1, true, raw_cw);
config_nand_cw_read(chip, false, raw_cw);
```
Reason:
The fix involves using the variable `raw_cw`, which is adjusted to account for the new register for the last code word when QPIC V2 is detected. This ensures that the correct code word is read from the NAND controller, preventing the misinterpretation that led to the bug.


